(4248437, 607614, 83569, '<td valign="top">Thank you for the input. The "wire" in the back is actually a fold in the backdrop since I set it up to look very flow-y. However, when I changed the brightness and contrast of the picture, all of the other folds pretty much faded but that one that caught the most light still remained. Also, the "scratch" in the glass is actually a reflection of my tripod which I had no clue how to hide. Any suggestions for next time?<br/>Thank you all for the comments and suggestions.</td>', 'Thank you for the input. The "wire" in the back is actually a fold in the backdrop since I set it up to look very flow-y. However, when I changed the brightness and contrast of the picture, all of the other folds pretty much faded but that one that caught the most light still remained. Also, the "scratch" in the glass is actually a reflection of my tripod which I had no clue how to hide. Any suggestions for next time?Thank you all for the comments and suggestions.', '2007-11-15 00:41:21.000000', NULL, 0),
